  "result": {
    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `simplify` function:\n\n```python\ndef simplify(x, n):\n\n\"\"\"Returns True if the fractions multiply out to a whole number.\"\"\"\n    # Convert the fractions to integers\n    x1, x2 = map(int, x.split('/'))\n    n1, n2 = map(int, n.split('/'))\n    \n    # Calculate the product of the fractions\n    product = x1 * x2 / n1 * n2\n    \n    # Check if the product is a whole number\n    return product == int(product)\n```\n\nThis function first converts the input strings representing fractions to integers by extracting the numerator and denominator. It then calculates the product of the fractions and checks if the result is a whole number. If it is not, the function returns `True`; otherwise, it returns `False`.",
